the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Answer 1 of *a case* is *a text*; scenario element.
    the Answer 2 of *a case* is *a text*; scenario element.
    the Answer 3 of *a case* is *a text*; scenario element.
    root holds for *a case*.
    One holds for *a case*.
    Two holds for *a case*.
    Three holds for *a case*.
    child *a number* of root counts for *a case*.
    root is decided for *a case*.
    root would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    One is decided for *a case*.
    Two is decided for *a case*.
    Three is decided for *a case*.
    One would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Two would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Three would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r3_6_evaluation_delegated_three_queried_children includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/evaluation-delegated-three-queried-children.ruml".

child 1 of root counts for a case if
    One holds for the case.

child 2 of root counts for a case if
    Two holds for the case.

child 3 of root counts for a case if
    Three holds for the case.

% Two or more are true
root holds for a case if
    root is decided for the case
    and a number M is the count of each N such that
        child a number N of root counts for the case
    and M >= 2.

root holds for a case if
    it is not the case that root is decided for the case
    and root would hold for the case.

root is decided for a case if
    One is decided for the case
    and Two is decided for the case
    and Three is decided for the case.

One holds for a case if
    the Answer 1 of the case is "yes".

One holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Answer 1 of the case is "yes"
    and it is not the case that the Answer 1 of the case is "no"
    and One would hold for the case.

One is decided for a case if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the Answer 1 of the case is "yes"
        and it is not the case that the Answer 1 of the case is "no".

Two holds for a case if
    the Answer 2 of the case is "yes".

Two holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Answer 2 of the case is "yes"
    and it is not the case that the Answer 2 of the case is "no"
    and Two would hold for the case.

Two is decided for a case if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the Answer 2 of the case is "yes"
        and it is not the case that the Answer 2 of the case is "no".

Three holds for a case if
    the Answer 3 of the case is "yes".

Three holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Answer 3 of the case is "yes"
    and it is not the case that the Answer 3 of the case is "no"
    and Three would hold for the case.

Three is decided for a case if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the Answer 3 of the case is "yes"
        and it is not the case that the Answer 3 of the case is "no".

